## Implementation Details

The Analytics component is correctly integrated in the root layout (`web/app/layout.tsx`):

```typescript
import { Analytics as VercelAnalytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        <AuthProvider>{children}</AuthProvider>
        <Analytics />           {/* Custom analytics component */}
        <VercelAnalytics />    {/* Vercel Web Analytics */}
        <BackendStatusBanner />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## Notes
- The project uses Next.js with App Router (confirmed by `app/layout.tsx` structure)
- The package manager is npm (confirmed by `package-lock.json`)
- The setup matches the latest official documentation requirements
- No additional configuration is needed - ready for use once enabled in Vercel dashboard

## Next Steps for Project Owner
To enable Web Analytics:
1. Go to your Vercel dashboard
2. Navigate to your project settings
3. Enable Web Analytics feature
4. Deploy the application
5. Analytics data will automatically start collecting

The code implementation is complete and production-ready.
